cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, datasets, or surrogate models in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "HemoDyn-AI: Physics-Guided Machine Learning and CFD for Arterial Stenosis Hemodynamics"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
url: "https://github.com/z5rcnws7bz-eng/HemoDyn-Ai"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ron"
    given-names: "Jace"
    affiliation: "Temple University"
    orcid: ""
keywords:
  - "hemodynamics"
  - "computational-fluid-dynamics"
  - "physics-guided-machine-learning"
  - "arterial-stenosis"
  - "simvascular"
  - "surrogate-modeling"
  - "wall-shear-stress"
  - "scientific-machine-learning"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  HemoDyn-AI is a reproducible computational hemodynamics and physics-guided
  machine learning framework for evaluating arterial blood flow in healthy and
  stenotic arteries (0%, 30%, 50%, and 70% diameter constrictions). By coupling
  Navier-Stokes solutions from SimVascular svSolver with gradient-boosted
  residual surrogate models, HemoDyn-AI achieves fast, highly accurate
  approximations of 3D velocity fields, pressure drops, and wall shear stress (WSS)
  with spatial and cross-geometry holdout validation.

